{
  "_README": [
    "THE PLANNED-TABLES JOIN — G4417, 5 Oct 2026. Until this file the C4 page carried",
    "six hand-typed cards of table names from docs/persistence-design.md §2, captioned",
    "'designed, no DDL yet', while the tree had built ninety-eight of its own. Nothing",
    "joined the plan to the build, so a planned name that SHIPPED read as unbuilt and",
    "one that never would read as owed.",
    "",
    "Each entry: `planned` is the name §2 used; `status` is one of",
    "  same      — built under that name;",
    "  renamed   — built under another name, same thing;",
    "  reshaped  — built, but as a different shape (named in `note`);",
    "  absent    — no table exists for it.",
    "`builtAs` is `plane:schema.name` (plane is `data` or `control`) and is null for",
    "`absent`. check-c4-freshness.mjs FAILS when a builtAs table is missing, and when",
    "an `absent` entry's planned name now exists as a table in either database.",
    "",
    "A built table that is no entry's builtAs must be listed in c4-acknowledged.json",
    "or the gate fails — an unclassified table is how this list rots."
  ],
  "tables": [
